---
import RngChordsApp from "../app/RngChordsApp";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../styles/app.css";

const pageTitle = "RNG Chords | Random Chord Generator";
const pageDescription =
	"Generate chord progressions for guitar, piano, songwriting, and production. Roll ideas, hear them instantly, keep the best chords, and export MIDI.";
const pageUrl = Astro.site
	? new URL("/", Astro.site).toString()
	: "https://rngchords.jonathanrreed.com/";
const socialImage = Astro.site
	? new URL("/social-card.svg", Astro.site).toString()
	: "/social-card.svg";
const authorSameAs = [
	"https://jonathanrreed.com/",
	"https://github.com/JonathanRReed",
];
const publishedDate = "2026-04-21";
const modifiedDate = "2026-10-21";
const author = {
	"@type": "Person",
	name: "Jonathan R. Reed",
	url: "https://jonathanrreed.com",
	sameAs: authorSameAs,
};

// Site-level JSON-LD describes the public tool without inventing independent
// ratings or reviews that do not exist.
const structuredData = {
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "WebSite",
	"@id": `${pageUrl}#website`,
	name: "RNG Chords",
	description: pageDescription,
	url: pageUrl,
	image: socialImage,
	isAccessibleForFree: true,
	inLanguage: "en-US",
	datePublished: publishedDate,
	dateModified: modifiedDate,
	author,
	creator: author,
};

// Project-level JSON-LD. The tool has no independent ratings or reviews, so it
// deliberately avoids the SoftwareApplication rich-result type.
const creativeWorkData = {
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "CreativeWork",
	"@id": `${pageUrl}#project`,
	name: "RNG Chords",
	description: pageDescription,
	url: pageUrl,
	image: socialImage,
	isAccessibleForFree: true,
	inLanguage: "en-US",
	datePublished: publishedDate,
	dateModified: modifiedDate,
	isPartOf: { "@id": `${pageUrl}#website` },
	keywords: "chord progression generator, songwriting, music production, MIDI export",
	author,
	creator: author,
};
---

<Base title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} path="/" jsonLd={[structuredData, creativeWorkData]} author>
	<RngChordsApp client:load />

	<section class="guide" aria-labelledby="how-it-works">
		<h2 id="how-it-works">How the chords are picked</h2>

		<p>
			Every roll starts with dice. In Easy mode each die becomes one chord, and
			its size (d4 up to d20) sets how far that chord can wander. Advanced mode
			uses five dice, one each for the root, quality, extensions, inversion,
			and rhythm. Manual mode skips the dice. Type something like
			<code>Cmaj9, Am11, D7b9, G13</code> or build a chord from parts.
		</p>

		<h3>The key</h3>
		<p>
			The dice total picks the key from nine centers: C, G, D, A, E, F, B&#9837;,
			E&#9837;, and A&#9837;. Every root comes from that key's major scale, and
			the quality is rolled separately. That's why a minor chord can land where
			a major one "should" be. The roots keep the progression grounded and the
			qualities bring the surprise.
		</p>
		<p>
			There's no minor-key switch. For something darker, keep the chords that
			fit and reroll the rest until the first one comes up minor.
		</p>

		<h3>Chord style</h3>
		<p>This setting changes what the dice can pick from. It doesn't change the key.</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Simple</strong> uses major, minor, and dominant chords with at
				most a 6, 7, or maj7 on top, in root position.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Color</strong> adds sus4, diminished, and augmented chords, plus
				9ths, 11ths, 13ths, and altered notes like &#9837;9 and &#9839;11.
				Inversions go up to the second.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Tension</strong> gives every chord an extension, allows
				inversions up to the third, and lets a chord shrink to an eighth note.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h3>Working with a roll</h3>
		<p>
			Press Space to hear it before you judge it. Tempo runs from 58 to 164
			BPM, and six sounds are built in, because a stack that's crowded on a
			bright piano can sit fine on a pad.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Keep</strong> pins a chord and <strong>Reroll unkept</strong>
			rolls the others, so you can hold two you like and hunt for the rest.
			Save versions to A, B, or C to compare takes. <strong>Export MIDI</strong>
			writes a .mid file with the tempo already set.
		</p>
		<p>
			Everything happens in your browser, and your last idea is saved in local
			storage. It's free, with no account. More background is on the
			<a href="/about/">about page</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<SiteFooter />
</Base>
